  "lineage": "Anatolian long-necked lute practice at the center of Turkish and Alevi folk music, transmitted through the aşık bards from Pir Sultan Abdal and Karacaoğlan to Âşık Veysel and Neşet Ertaş — fretted with microtonal ties for makam-derived ayak modes, played with plectrum or bare-fingered şelpe, sustaining an open-string drone beneath a melody in 2/4 or aksak 5/8, 7/8 and 9/8, most often self-accompanying a solo declaimed verse.",
